        <property key="7405">
          <object type="sn.model.model.Node">
            <property key="db" ref="4914533376" />
            <property key="individual" type="bool" value="True" />
            <property key="attributes">
              <object type="util.persistence.serialize.strdict">
                <property key="name">
                  <object type="util.attribute.Attribute">
                    <property key="value">
                      <object type="str" value="Label templates: what an object's label says, as a string w…" />
                    </property>
                    <property key="type" type="str" value="None" />
                    <property key="restriction" type="str" value="None" />
                  </object>
                </property>
                <property key="text">
                  <object type="util.attribute.Attribute">
                    <property key="value">
                      <object type="str" value="Label templates: what an object's label says, as a string with shell-style&#10;(POSIX parameter expansion) substitutions:&#10;&#10;  ``$key`` or ``${key}``    the value of *key*&#10;  ``${key:+text}``          *text* if *key* has a (non-empty) value, else nothing&#10;  ``${key:-text}``          *key*'s value, or *text* if it has none&#10;  ``$$``                    a &quot;$&quot;&#10;  ``\n``                    a line break&#10;  ``$(module:function)``    what a hook returns (see *sn.hooks*): eg: source code&#10;&#10;*text* may itself contain substitutions, and *key* may be a hook's call:&#10;``${(module:function):+text}`` is *text* if the hook returns something. Keys (see *labelLookup()*) are any&#10;attribute of the object (its effective value), and:&#10;&#10;  ``name``         its name&#10;  ``localName``    its name only if it has its own (not one inherited)&#10;  ``type``         the names of its types (parents), comma separated&#10;  ``constraints``  a variable's constraints (see *sn.model.constraints*)&#10;  ``id``           its id&#10;&#10;Eg: ``$name${constraints:+ {$constraints}}`` gives &quot;fred&quot; or &quot;?p {alive}&quot;;&#10;``$type${name:+: $name}`` gives Sowa's &quot;person: fred&quot;.&#10;&#10;The template is the object's &quot;vis/label&quot; attribute if it has one (eg: set on a&#10;type, for all its instances), else the &quot;gui/label&quot; preference (&quot;gui/relationLabel&quot;&#10;for relations). Tooltips are templates too: &quot;vis/tooltip&quot;, else &quot;gui/tooltip&quot;&#10;(see *DEFAULT_TOOLTIP*). A hook is called each time the template is expanded&#10;-- for a label, each time it's drawn -- so a slow one is better in a tooltip.&#10;&#10;Created on Sep 29, 2026&#10;&#10;.. codeauthor:: Rob Kremer &lt;robkremer@me.com&gt;" />
                    </property>
                    <property key="type" type="str" value="None" />
                    <property key="restriction" type="str" value="None" />
                  </object>
                </property>
              </object>
            </property>
            <property key="inferred" type="bool" value="False" />
          </object>
        </property>
        <property key="7406">
          <object type="sn.model.model.IsaIndividual">
            <property key="db" ref="4914533376" />
            <property key="attributes">
