                <property key="text">
                  <object type="util.attribute.Attribute">
                    <property key="value">
                      <object type="str" value="The order to show attributes in, grouped by the parts of their names (see&#10;*GROUP_SEPARATOR*), like a tree of folders: at each level, the names with no&#10;more separators first, then each group -- its header, and then its own&#10;contents, likewise -- all sorted (ignoring case). Eg: &quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;a/a&quot;, &quot;a/b&quot;,&#10;&quot;a/a/a&quot;, &quot;a/a/b&quot;, &quot;b/a&quot; are shown as::&#10;&#10;  a&#10;  b&#10;  a/      (a group)&#10;    a/a&#10;    a/b&#10;    a/a/    (a group)&#10;      a/a/a&#10;      a/a/b&#10;  b/      (a group)&#10;    b/a&#10;&#10;:param keys: The attribute names.&#10;:type keys: list[str]&#10;:returns: (kind, name, depth) for each line: kind is &quot;key&quot; (name is an&#10;  attribute's name) or &quot;group&quot; (name is the group's path, eg: &quot;a/a&quot;).&#10;:rtype: list[tuple[str, str, int]]" />
                    </property>
                    <property key="type" type="str" value="None" />
                    <property key="restriction" type="str" value="None" />
                  </object>
                </property>
              </object>
            </property>
            <property key="inferred" type="bool" value="False" />
          </object>
        </property>
